{
  "id": "COMPOUND:934 - DISEASE:3180",
  "verbalization": "Isoniazid appears to influence a series of molecular pathways that ultimately lead to a condition associated with Toddler. The drug affects microRNA 4259, which in turn causes Down Syndrome, a condition linked to solute carrier family 5 member 10, which further contributes to Toddler. Similarly, Isoniazid impacts an olfactory receptor pseudogene, which causes Tremor, a condition that also leads to Toddler. These pathways highlight a complex interplay where Isoniazid's effects are mediated through multiple molecular mechanisms, ultimately contributing to a developmental condition in Toddler. The evidence suggests that Isoniazid may have a role in the pathogenesis of Toddler through these indirect pathways, though the exact mechanism by which Isoniazid influences these downstream effects remains to be fully elucidated.",
